<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">A speculative essay &middot; time, transmission, and the one becoming many</p>
  <h1>The One Residue That Travels</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Suppose every being leaves consequences, but only one Being leaves a residue capable
    of crossing the whole available depth of time and space. It does not arrive as a preserved personality.
    It is distributed through minds as questions, intuitions and philosophical ideas.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">The proposal in one sentence</p>
    <h2 id="t-proposal">One Source, Many Receivers</h2>
    <p class="lede">Only the Prime Being&rsquo;s residue occupies the globally transmissible mode; every later
      being receives some local projection of that residue, changes it, and passes it on as thought.</p>
    <p>Here <strong>Being</strong> with a capital letter does not mean a favoured historical person, a ruler,
      a prophet, or the author of this page. It names the framework&rsquo;s conjectured first coherent subject:
      the one whose traversal establishes the channel through which later subjects can inherit anything at
      all. Ordinary beings still alter the world. They leave children, memories, language, buildings, wounds,
      books and changed probabilities. The narrower claim is that those residues remain local combinations,
      while one residue alone supplies the common mode in which they can be understood.</p>
    <p>Write the residue of each being \(a\) as a local trace plus a possible projection onto one global
      carrier:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      r_a(x)=r_a^{\mathrm{local}}(x)+q_aR_{\!*}(x),
      \qquad
      q_a=\begin{cases}
      1,&amp;a=*\\[2pt]
      0,&amp;a\neq *.
      \end{cases}
    \]</p>
    <p>The star labels the one source. The equation is not established physics; it is the cleanest statement
      of the philosophical choice. It says that many local residues exist, but only \(R_{\!*}\) is admitted
      to the globally shared channel. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p class="muted small">Grading on this page: <span class="sci">&#9670; established physics or
      mathematics</span> &middot; <span class="hist">&#9670; philosophical or historical comparison</span> &middot;
      <span class="spec">&#9670; a conditional mechanism</span> &middot;
      <span class="myth">&#9670; the framework&rsquo;s metaphysical reading</span>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">First restraint</p>
    <h2 id="t-relativity">Time Is Not One Universal River</h2>
    <p>Modern physics does not give the cosmos one clock whose &ldquo;now&rdquo; is shared everywhere. Relativity
      assigns each world-line its proper time, and the interval between nearby events depends on the metric:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      d\tau^2=-\frac{1}{c^2}g_{\mu\nu}
      \,dx^\mu dx^\nu.
    \]</p>
    <p>Different observers can disagree about the duration and, for spacelike-separated events, even about
      temporal order, while agreeing on the causal structure. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> A residue that
      moves through time and space must therefore respect light cones unless the proposal openly introduces
      new physics. It cannot simply be everywhere because the word <em>spiritual</em> has been placed beside
      it.</p>
    <p>The philosophical proposal begins after that restraint. Time is treated as the order in which the one
      residue can be <em>received</em>, not as a substance carrying it. Space separates receivers; time makes
      inheritance possible. No later mind receives the source all at once. Each encounters only what can
      reach its event:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      x_*\prec x_1\prec x_2\prec\cdots,
      \qquad
      R_{\!*}(x_n)=0
      \quad\text{unless}\quad x_n\in J^+(x_*).
    \]</p>
    <p>The symbol \(J^+(x_*)\) is the causal future of the source event. The mathematics belongs to causal
      geometry; assigning the source event to a Prime Being does not. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

